# Parsed by Cloudflare Pages (and Netlify) out of the build output root; the
# file itself is never served. Rules are applied in file order and the headers
# of every matching rule are joined, so a narrower rule has to detach
# Cache-Control before setting its own value - otherwise the directives from
# the rule it narrows get appended and conflict.

# Every page is a fresh deploy's output, so let it show up on the next request
# instead of after a stale copy expires. This also covers HTML that is a note.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Image renditions are named after a hash of their source, so an edited image
# is always a new URL and these can be pinned for a year.
/img/optimized/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
